{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# CineDiff demo\n",
    "\n",
    "Reconstructs a small cine MRI example with the pretrained CineDiff model.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Before running:** choose *Runtime → Change runtime type → GPU*. The 8-frame\n",
    "example needs about 14 GB of GPU memory, which fits the free T4 (15 GB). The\n",
    "15-frame example needs about 26 GB (for example an A100)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!nvidia-smi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Settings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "REPO_URL = \"https://github.com/OSU-MR/CineDiff.git\"\n",
    "BRANCH = \"main\"\n",
    "CASE = \"fs_0008_1_5T_sli0_R16_8frames\"   # or \"fs_0008_1_5T_sli0_R16_15frames\"\n",
    "OUTPUT_ROOT = \"outputs/demo\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Get the code\n",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%cd /content\n",
    "!rm -rf CineDiff\n",
    "!git clone --single-branch --depth 1 --branch {BRANCH} {REPO_URL} CineDiff\n",
    "%cd /content/CineDiff\n",
    "!git log --oneline -1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Install dependencies\n",
    "\n",
    "Colab already has PyTorch, NumPy, SciPy, scikit-image, Matplotlib, and Pillow;\n",
    "this installs the remaining packages."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q einops==0.8.0 einops-exts==0.0.4 rotary-embedding-torch==0.6.4 lpips==0.1.4 DISTS-pytorch==0.1 tqdm"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Download the model weights\n",
    "\n",
    "The example cases are included in the repository, so only the weights (286 MB)\n",
    "are needed. They are checked against their SHA256."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python download.py --weights-only"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The DISTS metric looks for its own weights in Python's install prefix, where pip\n",
    "does not put them on Colab, so download them there.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, sys, urllib.request\n",
    "\n",
    "dists_weights = os.path.join(sys.prefix, \"weights.pt\")\n",
    "urllib.request.urlretrieve(\n",
    "    \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dingkeyan93/DISTS/master/DISTS_pytorch/weights.pt\",\n",
    "    dists_weights,\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(dists_weights, os.path.getsize(dists_weights), \"bytes\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Check the case settings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python reconstruct.py --case {CASE} --output-root {OUTPUT_ROOT} --devices 0 --dry-run"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Reconstruct\n",
    "\n",
    "Add `--avg 8` to average eight samples, as in the paper (about eight times\n",
    "longer), or `--nfe` to change the number of sampling steps."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python reconstruct.py --case {CASE} --output-root {OUTPUT_ROOT} --devices 0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from IPython.display import Image, display\n",
    "from PIL import Image as PILImage\n",
    "\n",
    "result = f\"{OUTPUT_ROOT}/{CASE}/evaluations/full_image\"\n",
    "display(pd.read_csv(f\"{result}/metrics.csv\")[[\"method\", \"snr\", \"psnr\", \"ssim\", \"lpips\", \"dists\"]])\n",
    "gif = f\"{result}/comparison.gif\"\n",
    "display(Image(filename=gif, width=PILImage.open(gif).width * 3.7 // 5))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Higher quality: posterior mean\n",
    "\n",
    "Looking for higher-quality images? Average several independent samples to get\n",
    "the posterior mean, as in the paper. `--avg 8` runs eight reconstructions one\n",
    "after another and averages them, so it takes about eight times as long; GPU\n",
    "memory stays the same."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python reconstruct.py --case {CASE} --output-root {OUTPUT_ROOT}_avg8 --devices 0 --avg 8"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "result_avg8 = f\"{OUTPUT_ROOT}_avg8/{CASE}/evaluations/full_image\"\n",
    "display(pd.read_csv(f\"{result_avg8}/metrics.csv\")[[\"method\", \"snr\", \"psnr\", \"ssim\", \"lpips\", \"dists\"]])\n",
    "gif_avg8 = f\"{result_avg8}/comparison.gif\"\n",
    "display(Image(filename=gif_avg8, width=PILImage.open(gif_avg8).width * 3.7 // 5))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## More cases (optional)\n",
    "\n",
    "The full dataset (1.1 GB) contains 56 fully sampled and 15 undersampled cases,\n",
    "listed in `data/cases.json`. The full-size cases need much more GPU memory\n",
    "than Colab's T4 provides.\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "!python download.py --data-only\n",
    "!python reconstruct.py --case fs_0008_1_5T_sli0_R16 --output-root {OUTPUT_ROOT}\n",
    "```"
   ]
  }
 ],
